{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LvTsA6uXEUuQT5oEgb3yQs","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"searched_issues\": 1477,\n  \"quarantined\": 0,\n  \"threshold\": 0.35,\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 1964,\n      \"score\": 0.331,\n      \"title\": \"How can I add speed process to rich.progress.track? Is it possible?\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Rich is wonderful, but I think it needs to be at least as good as '**tqdm**' is in a simple example. When I want to process data in for loops, I want to tell me about the **'speed'**. that speed helps me to improve performance. Also, I need the **'total time'** of the process at the end. Is it possible to add these items to ```rich.progress.track```? should I use different functions or libraries? This is my for loop: ``` for ndf_addr, image_addr in track(zip(ndfs_addr, images_addr), total=len(ndfs_addr), description=\\\"Processing data...\\\"): ... ```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 304,\n      \"score\": 0.328,\n      \"title\": \"[REQUEST] progress bar: round up task.speed\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"**How would you improve Rich?** I love `rich`'s `ProgressBar`, but I have a very small issue with it: I can't seem to find a way to display `task.speed` without all the decimal numbers. This is how I'm defining my `ProgressBar`: ``` progress = Progress( TextColumn( \\\"[bold magenta]Step {task.completed}/{task.total} - {task.speed} steps/s\\\" ), # \\\"[progress.description]{task.description}\\\", BarColumn(bar_width=None), \\\"\\u2022\\\", \\\"[progress.percentage]{task.percentage:>3.0f}%\\\", TimeRemainingColumn(), ) ``` But the `task.speed` get's printed with loads of decimal numbers which doesn't look great: ``` Step 4 ...\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2193,\n      \"score\": 0.285,\n      \"title\": \"[REQUEST] task.speed should be 0 instead of None when task starts\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Referring to #1772, I feel the more sensible behaviour is that `task.speed` should be 0 instead of `None` when starting. This would avoid the need to write a custom column to workaround the issue and would be more elegant.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 415,\n      \"score\": 0.244,\n      \"title\": \"fill table rows with dataframe rows\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Hi How to fill table rows with dataframe rows ?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3835,\n      \"score\": 0.244,\n      \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Enable Speed For while total is not None in TaskProgressColumn\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"NOTE: If a feature could be implemented in a third-party library, then it is unlikely to be accepted as part of the core library. NOTE: Feature requests will not be considered unless first approved in discussions (https://github.com/textualize/rich/discussions) **How would you improve Rich?** <img width=\\\"822\\\" height=\\\"567\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/600dce6d-152d-4b0e-bd96-05c4ba457436\\\" /> If we using TaskProgressColumn with `total is not None` progress, it will only render the percentages **What problem does it solve for you?** I used rich in a DL Training Scri ...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1595c09-ff28-4c38-a6e0-914d871bd1ee","uuid":"d1abdf93-289e-496c-9fb9-9abec058be16","timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:27:27.471Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"searched_issues\": 1477,\n  \"quarantined\": 0,\n  \"threshold\": 0.35,\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 1964